    "text": "Students can begin by signing up for the CIS department mailing list and reaching out to Magner Career Center to craft a resume. Also, join the club discord, which periodically posts information relevant to students. Within the academic setting, they should look internally and begin preparing for programs such as CTP or TTP. Time passes quickly, so it is crucial that they begin doing their due diligence from the start. Even if they are not eligible to apply for certain programs, it helps to understand the requirements and not a month before the application due date.\n\nThey should also understand classes alone are insufficient to land a tech gig. Aside from tech program previously mentioned, CodePath can be helpful in helping students learn new technologies and build tech portfolio. There may be other types of programs available, but the idea is to get involved as soon as possible. It may be difficult to do supplementary learning during the school year, so extended breaks are valuable opportunities that they should not squander. Summer breaks are great, since some programs run during that time and not the winter break. Even if a program is not available, try searching for materials online, reaching out to students, or even professors for recommendations,"
